# Merge behaviour. See `docs/DECISIONS_LEDGER.md` D0298.
#
# The ledger is APPEND-ONLY by rule: `CLAUDE.md` forbids editing or reusing an entry number, because the
# numbers are addresses cited from commit messages, docs and code comments. Two branches that each append
# an entry therefore conflict on every rebase, always in the same way, always resolved the same way --
# keep both. `merge=union` is git's own resolver for exactly that file shape: it concatenates both sides'
# hunks in order, leaves no markers, and needs no human.
#
# Union merge is only safe because the append-only rule holds, and it fails SILENTLY if that rule is ever
# broken -- it will produce a file with one entry in it twice and report success. So it ships together
# with `tools/layer_lint/check_ledger_integrity.py`, which faults a number declared twice, a back-
# reference to an entry no longer present, and a conflict marker committed into the file. Enabling the
# resolver without that gate would be trading a loud, frequent conflict for a quiet, rare corruption,
# which is the wrong direction for this project specifically.
#
# Deliberately NOT applied to `docs/WORKING.md`, `docs/BRIEF.md` or the other normative docs: those are
# edited in place, so a union merge would duplicate prose rather than preserve appends. This line covers
# the one file whose append-only discipline is actually enforced.
docs/DECISIONS_LEDGER.md merge=union
